  "output": "Here is a full performance analysis with actionable fixes:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: HR Policy Bot\n\n### 1. N+1 Database Connection Anti-Pattern (HIGH)\n\n**`src/data/db.py` — every method opens a new `aiosqlite` connection**\n\nEach of the ~12 methods does:\n```python\nasync with aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path) as db:\n    ...\n```\n\nA single query triggers `save_query()` + `save_orchestrator_response()` + reads — 4+ new SQLite connections per request.\n\n**Fix — add a shared connection pool:**\n\n```python\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    _connection: aiosqlite.Connection | None = None\n\n    async def _get_conn(self) -> aiosqlite.Connection:\n        if self._connection is None or not self._connection.is_alive():\n            self._connection = await aiosqlite.connect(self._db_path)\n            self._connection.row_factory = aiosqlite.Row\n        return self._connection\n\n    async def save_query(self, record: QueryRecord) -> None:\n        db = await self._get_conn()\n        await db.execute(\"INSERT INTO ...\", (...))\n        await db.commit()\n```\n\nOr use a connection context manager that reuses a module-level singleton.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Policy Registry Loaded 8× at Startup (HIGH)\n\n**`src/agents/specialist.py` — `_load_instruments()` is called once per specialist instance**\n\n```python\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:           # ← disk read x8\n        registry = json.load(f)               # ← parse x8\n    return [r for r in registry if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\nAll 8 specialists are instantiated at startup (`get_specialists()`), so the 57 KB JSON file is read and deserialized 8 times.\n\n**Fix — cache the registry at module level:**\n\n```python\nimport functools\n\n@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=1)\ndef _load_registry() -> list[dict]:\n    with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    return [r for r in _load_registry() if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Per-Request DatabaseManager Instantiation (HIGH)\n\n**`src/api/routes.py` — new `DatabaseManager()` on every API request (lines 125, 138, 168, 179)**\n\n```python\n@router.get(\"/queries\")\nasync def list_queries(limit: int = Query(50, ...)):\n    db = DatabaseManager()   # ← new instance every GET /queries\n    queries = await db.list_queries(limit=limit)\n```\n\nInconsistent with `websocket.py` which uses a module-level singleton.\n\n**Fix — use FastAPI dependency injection:**\n\n```python\n# src/data/db.py\n_db: DatabaseManager | None = None\n\ndef get_db() -> DatabaseManager:\n    global _db\n    if _db is None:\n        _db = DatabaseManager()\n    return _db\n\n# src/api/routes.py\nfrom fastapi import Depends\nfrom src.data.db import get_db\n\n@router.get(\"/queries\")\nasync def list_queries(limit: int = Query(50), db: DatabaseManager = Depends(get_db)):\n    return await db.list_queries(limit=limit)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. LLM Response Not Cached (MEDIUM)\n\n**`src/llm/client.py` — identical queries call Gemini every time**\n\nThe LLM client has no caching. If the orchestrator falls back to all-8-agents mode and two queries arrive with the same text, both call the API twice.\n\n**Fix — TTL cache on `chat()` with a stable key:**\n\n```python\nfrom cachetools import TTLCache\nimport hashlib\n\n_response_cache: TTLCache = TTLCache(maxsize=256, ttl=3600)\n\nasync def chat(self, system_prompt: str, user_message: str, model: str | None = None) -> str:\n    cache_key = hashlib.sha256(f\"{system_prompt}|{user_message}|{model}\".encode()).hexdigest()\n    if cache_key in _response_cache:\n        return _response_cache[cache_key]\n    result = await self._generate(system_prompt, user_message, model)\n    _response_cache[cache_key] = result\n    return result\n```\n\nAdd `cachetools` to `requirements.txt`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Global Domain Lock Serializes All Fetch Requests (MEDIUM)\n\n**`src/fetch/engine.py` lines 81–86 — single lock for all domain timing**\n\n```python\nasync with self._domain_lock:          # ← one lock for ALL domains\n    last_request = self._domain_last_request[domain]\n    delay_required = 1.0 - (time.time() - last_request)\n    if delay_required > 0:\n        await asyncio.sleep(delay_required)   # ← sleeps while holding lock\n```\n\nDomain A sleeping 1 second blocks all concurrent fetches for domains B–H.\n\n**Fix — per-domain locks (you already have `_domain_semaphores`, extend it):**\n\n```python\nself._domain_locks: dict[str, asyncio.Lock] = defaultdict(asyncio.Lock)\n\n# In _apply_rate_limit():\nasync with self._domain_locks[domain]:\n    last_request = self._domain_last_request[domain]\n    delay_required = 1.0 - (time.time() - last_request)\n    if delay_required > 0:\n        await asyncio.sleep(delay_required)\n    self._domain_last_request[domain] = time.time()\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. `_domain_last_request` Grows Unbounded (MEDIUM / Memory Leak)\n\n**`src/fetch/engine.py` line 48** — `defaultdict(float)` never cleaned up.\n\nEvery unique domain fetched during the process lifetime is added permanently. Not a crisis for this workload (fixed policy domains), but worth capping.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```python\nfrom cachetools import TTLCache\nself._domain_last_request: TTLCache = TTLCache(maxsize=1000, ttl=3600)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Citations Iterated Twice Per Response (LOW)\n\n**`src/agents/orchestrator.py` — `_build_synthesis_prompt()` and `_aggregate_citations()` both loop over the same specialist responses**\n\n```python\n# First pass — build synthesis prompt (line ~185)\nfor response in specialist_responses:\n    for citation in response.get(\"citations\", []):\n        parts.append(f\"  - {citation.get('instrument_title')}\")\n\n# Second pass — deduplicate citations (line ~206)\ndef _aggregate_citations(self, specialist_responses):\n    for resp in specialist_responses:\n        for c in resp.get(\"citations\", []):\n            key = (c.get(\"instrument_title\", \"\"), c.get(\"url\", \"\"))\n```\n\n**Fix — extract citations once:**\n\n```python\ndef _process_responses(self, specialist_responses):\n    all_citations = [\n        c for resp in specialist_responses\n        for c in resp.get(\"citations\", [])\n    ]\n    # use all_citations in both synthesis prompt building and aggregation\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. Frontend: Redundant DOM Queries on Feedback Click (LOW)\n\n**`static/js/app.js` lines 391–400 — inner loop re-queries DOM on every click**\n\n```javascript\ndocument.querySelectorAll('.feedback-buttons .btn-feedback').forEach(btn => {\n    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        // Queries DOM again inside the click handler:\n        document.querySelectorAll('.feedback-buttons .btn-feedback').forEach(b => {\n            b.classList.remove('selected');\n            b.style.opacity = '0.5';    // ← triggers reflow per element\n            b.disabled = true;\n        });\n    });\n});\n```\n\n**Fix — capture buttons once, batch style with a class:**\n\n```javascript\nconst feedbackBtns = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.feedback-buttons .btn-feedback'));\nfeedbackBtns.forEach(btn => {\n    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        feedbackBtns.forEach(b => b.classList.replace('selected', 'unselected'));\n        btn.classList.add('selected');\n    });\n});\n```\n\n```css\n.btn-feedback.unselected { opacity: 0.5; pointer-events: none; }\n.btn-feedback.selected   { opacity: 1.0; }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. WebSocket Status Updates Without Deduplication (LOW)\n\n**`static/js/app.js` `handleAgentStatusUpdate()`** — no guard against repeated identical status.\n\n```javascript\nfunction handleAgentStatusUpdate(data) {\n    const agentItem = agentList.querySelector(`[data-agent=\"${data.agent_id}\"]`);\n    if (agentItem) {\n        const statusDot = agentItem.querySelector('.status-dot');\n        statusDot.setAttribute('data-status', data.status);  // ← updates DOM unconditionally\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```javascript\nconst agentStatusCache = {};\nfunction handleAgentStatusUpdate(data) {\n    if (agentStatusCache[data.agent_id] === data.status) return;\n    agentStatusCache[data.agent_id] = data.status;\n    const agentItem = agentList.querySelector(`[data-agent=\"${data.agent_id}\"]`);\n    if (agentItem) {\n        agentItem.querySelector('.status-dot').setAttribute('data-status', data.status);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. Broken `CacheEntry.fetched_at` Property (CRITICAL)\n\n**`src/fetch/cache.py` lines 24–31** — `fetched_at` is referenced in a `@property` but never declared as a dataclass field.\n\nThis will raise `AttributeError` the first time a cached entry's TTL is evaluated (i.e., every cache hit check).\n\n**Fix — add the missing field to the dataclass:**\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass CacheEntry:\n    url: str\n    content: str\n    content_type: str\n    status_code: int\n    ttl_hours: int\n    fetched_at: datetime | str    # ← add this\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| # | File | Issue | Effort |\n|---|------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | `src/fetch/cache.py:24` | `fetched_at` missing — broken at runtime | 1 line |\n| 2 | `src/data/db.py` | New connection per method call | Medium |\n| 3 | `src/agents/specialist.py` | Registry loaded 8× | 5 lines |\n| 4 | `src/api/routes.py` | DB instance per request | Small |\n| 5 | `src/fetch/engine.py:81` | Global domain lock | Small |\n| 6 | `src/llm/client.py` | No LLM response cache | Medium |\n| 7 | `src/agents/orchestrator.py` | Double citation iteration | Small |\n| 8 | `static/js/app.js:391` | DOM re-query on click | Small |\n| 9 | `static/js/app.js` | Status update deduplication | Small |\n| 10 | `src/fetch/engine.py:48` | Unbounded domain dict | Small |\n\nItems 1 and 3 are the quickest wins — fix #1 immediately (it's actively broken), and fix #3 to cut startup I/O by 7/8ths. Item 2 (connection pooling) will have the largest impact on query latency.\n",
